{title: Go, Tell It on the Mountain}
{artist: Traditional spiritual}
{genre: Gospel, Christmas}
{flow: Closing}
{style: Spiritual}
{key: F}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Go, tell it on the mountain
Over the [Bb]hills and every[F]where
Go, tell it on the mountain
That [C7]Jesus Christ is [F]born
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
While [F]shepherds kept their watching
O'er [Bb]silent flocks by [F]night
Behold, throughout the heavens
There [C7]shone a holy [F]light
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The [F]shepherds feared and trembled
When [Bb]lo! above the [F]earth
Rang out the angel chorus
That [C7]hailed our Saviour's [F]birth
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Down [F]in a lowly manger
The [Bb]humble Christ was [F]born
And God sent us salvation
That [C7]blessed Christmas [F]morn
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
